Package: GeoModelR
Title: Tools for Phylogenetic Geographic Modelling and Biogeographic Analysis
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Jorge", "Avaria-Llautureo",
           email = "j.l.avaria@reading.ac.uk",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-8610-7428")),
    person("Andrew", "Meade", role = "ctb",
           comment = "Co-author of clean_sister_geodata()")
    )
Description: Tools for the Geographical (Geo) model implemented in
    'BayesTraits' v5+, which reconstructs ancestral geographic locations
    on a phylogeny, optionally restricted to land or sea on palaeomaps.
    Covers three workflows: (1) input data checks, removing overlapping
    coordinates of sister taxa that can compress branches to zero length;
    (2) palaeomap preparation, downloading palaeocoastlines from the
    'GPlates' Web Service and writing land/ocean grids and 'BuildMaps'
    files for 'BayesTraits'; and (3) output exploration, reading
    'AncStates' files, plotting posterior ancestral locations on
    age-matched palaeomaps, and computing posterior dispersal distances in
    the palaeo or plate reference frame. Described in Avaria-Llautureo et
    al. (2025) <doi:10.1073/pnas.2423833122>.
